<title>JAPAN: Japan March raw sugar imports fall 21.3 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Japan March raw sugar imports fall 21.3 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-04-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's raw sugar imports in March totalled 67,260 tonnes, down by 21.3 percent from a year earlier, Finance Ministry data released on Monday showed.</p>
<p>The breakdown was as follows (in tonnes):</p>
<p>			   Mar 97     Feb 97	  Mar 96</p>
<p> Total		   67,260     62,072	  85,490</p>
<p>Main suppliers:</p>
<p> Thailand		33,223     45,803	  52,050</p>
<p> Australia	     30,643     16,269	  33,440</p>
<p> Cuba		     3,394	  nil	     nil</p>
<p> South Africa	     nil	  nil	     nil</p>
<p>Total imports in the first three months of calendar 1997 reached 241,544 tonnes, against 287,909 tonnes during the same period of last year.</p>
<p>-- Tokyo Commodities Desk (+81-3-3432-7391)</p>
</text>
